{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during your stay. You were brought in because of high blood sugar and weakness. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m still tired. I was so sluggish yesterday morning, and my blood sugar was way too high. My daughter called the office, and they told her to give me insulin and bring me in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood sugar was 350 when you arrived. We checked your labs, and while it’s high, there’s no sign of ketoacidosis. Did you miss any insulin doses?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I fell asleep early and forgot my nighttime glargine. Then I had a big breakfast—sausage, grits, toast. I didn’t think it would be that bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That explains it. Missing your long-acting insulin and then eating a high-carb meal can spike your sugar. We’ll restart your insulin and monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been trying, but sometimes I forget or just don’t feel like taking it all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. You have a lot of medications. That’s something we’ll talk about later. For now, your kidney function is a bit worse than usual—creatinine is 3.2—but it’s likely due to the high sugar and mild dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My kidneys are always a little off. But it usually comes back down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your baseline is around 1.6 to 2.0, so this is elevated but not unexpected. We’ll keep an eye on it. Also, your hemoglobin is low at 8.1, but no sign of bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been anemic for years. My doctor says it’s from my liver and kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We won’t treat it now since it’s stable. One more thing—we did a chest X-ray, and there’s a small opacity in your left lung. Did you have any cough or fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no cough. I did feel a little chilled yesterday, but that’s it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows a possible lingular infiltrate, but you’re not running a fever, and your white count is normal. We don’t think it’s pneumonia, so we’re not starting antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a reaction to levofloxacin before—itching. I’m glad you’re not giving it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we noted your allergy. We gave one dose in the ER, but stopped it due to the reaction. No more will be given."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And my liver? I know it’s always a concern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound. Your liver looks stable—no new masses, blood vessels are open, and only a little fluid around it. Your tacrolimus levels are stable, so no signs of rejection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my hepatitis C? I know it came back after transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your viral load is still high, but we’re not starting treatment now. It’s being monitored by your transplant team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my seizures? I was supposed to start Keppra last time, but I never picked it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you had a seizure episode recently. We want you to stay on Keppra 500 mg twice a day. It helps prevent further seizures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try to remember. But my hands shake a lot—could that be from the Keppra or my tacrolimus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-06-17 18:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tremor could be from tacrolimus. Neurology thinks it’s likely related. But we won’t change it now since your liver is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar last night was 257. We tried giving your glargine in the morning, but your daytime sugars are better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been having low sugars in the morning. I wake up shaky sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked—your AM sugars were as low as 60, even though you’re not feeling it. That’s dangerous. We’re adjusting your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually eat a snack at night to prevent that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re splitting your glargine—10 units in the morning, 8 at bedtime. And we’re reducing your sliding scale at breakfast. We’ll stop the bedtime insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better. My old glucometer is so small—I can’t see the numbers well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The diabetes team gave you a new one with a larger screen. They also reviewed carb counting with you, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-06-18 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they did. I’ll try to be more consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-06-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugars are improving—morning levels are now in the 100s. Your creatinine is also coming down to 2.4. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-06-19 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m getting better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-06-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your lung opacity hasn’t changed, but you’re not sick, so we’re not worried. No fever, no cough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-06-19 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t feel any different in my chest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-06-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your labs this morning are stable. Creatinine is 2.2, glucose 130, hemoglobin 8.5—slightly better. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if all stays well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-06-20 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. But I’m nervous about managing everything at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-06-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve arranged home health services. A nurse will help you with meds and blood sugar checks. You shouldn’t be alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-06-20 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. My sisters want me to move in with them. I’m thinking about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-06-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could help. Your care is complex, and support makes a big difference."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more day. Your sugars are steady, and you’ve had no issues. We’ll finalize your discharge plan tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still take Keppra?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice a day. It’s important for seizure prevention. And your tacrolimus stays the same—1 mg morning and night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "10 units glargine at breakfast, 8 at bedtime. Plus your humalog as needed. The sliding scale is less aggressive now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my blood pressure and stomach meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—metoprolol, furosemide, ranitidine. All the same. We stopped the daily gabapentin—now it’s every other day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-06-21 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can manage that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-06-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your discharge is approved for tomorrow. We’ll go over all your meds and instructions today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-06-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2197-06-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your physical exam is much improved. You’re alert, moving well, and your lungs are clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2197-06-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eyes and bones?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2197-06-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using your latanoprost drops for glaucoma. And continue calcium and vitamin D for your osteopenia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2197-06-23 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. Your labs are stable—creatinine 2.2, glucose 133. You’re ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2197-06-23 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready, but a little nervous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2197-06-23 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The home health nurse will visit tomorrow. They’ll help with meds and check your blood sugar. Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2197-06-23 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll try not to miss my insulin again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2197-06-23 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. You’ve made great progress. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2197-06-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick call to check in. How are you doing at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2197-06-24 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The nurse came. She helped me organize my pills. I took my insulin on time this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2197-06-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Keep using your new glucometer and follow the sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2197-06-24 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I talked to my sisters. I’m going to move in with them next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2197-06-24 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. More support will help you stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2197-06-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final follow-up call. Your lab results from yesterday show your creatinine is 2.3 and glucose 140. Still doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2197-06-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling good. No shakiness, no confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2197-06-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Keep taking Keppra and all your meds. See your doctors in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2197-06-25 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2197-06-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and stay safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2197-06-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming your discharge is complete and you’re settled. Any issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2197-06-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "All good. My sisters helped me unpack. I took my morning insulin already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2197-06-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wonderful. We’re glad to hear it. Call us anytime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2197-06-26 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2197-06-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2197-06-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last message: your case manager will call this week to check on your transition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2197-06-26 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll be here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2197-06-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re here for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2197-06-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a reminder to keep your follow-up appointments with neurology and transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2197-06-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have them on my calendar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2197-06-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2197-06-26 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final note: your urine and blood cultures were negative. No infection found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2197-06-26 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2197-06-26 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No need. You’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2197-06-26 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll close your chart now. Call us if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2197-06-26 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2197-06-26 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-06-17 18:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-06-26 16:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 72-year-old woman with a history of liver transplant for HCV cirrhosis, type 2 diabetes, chronic kidney disease, and prior seizure was admitted for hyperglycemia and generalized weakness after missing her bedtime insulin and consuming a high-carbohydrate breakfast. Initial evaluation revealed a blood glucose of 350, elevated creatinine of 3.2, and mild anemia, with a chest X-ray showing a lingular opacity that was not treated due to lack of infection signs. She was managed with insulin regimen adjustments, splitting glargine to morning and bedtime doses to address recurrent morning hypoglycemia, and was restarted on levetiracetam for seizure prevention. Her kidney function improved to baseline, blood sugar stabilized, and she was discharged home with home health services, a revised medication plan, and plans to move in with family for better support.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with other specified manifestations, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Complications of transplanted liver",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Cirrhosis of liver without mention of alcohol",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage I through stage IV, or unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified glaucoma",
      "Disorder of bone and cartilage, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Essential and other specified forms of tremor",
      "Personal history of tobacco use"
    ]
  }
}
